(project pricklypear-workout
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: workout journal — fluid program documents + standardized journal facts")
 (status implemented)
 (* agent note (|2026-08-02 status reconcile: libs/workout/lib.pp (~2.6k lines) seeded; live (workout/programs) => free/ksk1/ksk2/ksk3; session-list/volume/home-page present. All chapter subsections match shipped package.|) *)
 (convention ocaml-dune)
 (section workout

  (doc "Training journal: programs as fluid trees, sessions/exercises as queryable facts, plan/run/capture packages")
  (status implemented)
  (verify
   (build "dune build image")
   (smoke "(load-library \"workout\") installs workout/… bindings and routes")
   (smoke "GET /workout lists recent sessions + start controls")
   (smoke "start free or program session creates workout-session in_progress with doc")
   (smoke "log exercise facts on a session; volume query returns totals")
   (smoke "complete session sets state complete and keeps exercise rows")
   (smoke "resume in_progress session restores doc progress")
   (smoke "pp_eval workout/session-list and workout/volume work for agents")
   (smoke "seed_stdlib can load workout after calendar (or documented order)"))

  (details
   (doc (|
        =========================================================
        PRODUCT INTENT
        =========================================================
        A first-class training journal on the live image.

        Domain tension (the whole design):
          - Workouts / programs are extremely fluid (ladders, intervals,
            dice, unilateral switches, freestyle blocks, rest schemes).
          - Journal analytics must stay boring and queryable
            (volume by exercise+load over a date range, streak of days
            trained, what I did last Tuesday).

        Resolution: hybrid model, two layers deliberately:
          1. FLUID DOCUMENT  — sexp/json tree for program structure and
             live run state. JSON and sexps are the same tree algebra;
             storage print form is an implementation detail.
          2. JOURNAL FACTS   — standardized workout-session +
             workout-exercise data_rows projected from the document
             (and/or quick-log UI) for history queries.

        Inspired by:
          - paper training logs (date, work done, notes)
          - Simple program runners (KSK, Q&D, custom blocks)
          - Pricklypear: objects in Postgres, UI as Nopales routes,
            agents log/query via eval — no parallel REST API

        NOT a social fitness network.
        NOT a wearable/HR integration platform.
        NOT an OCaml system page — this is a product package (Nopales).
        NOT a pure document store (that fails volume queries).
        NOT a fully normalized interval/rung schema (that fails fluidity).

        Killer property: the same capture functions humans hit from
        /workout are what agents call via pp_eval.

        Prior design note (habitat, design-paused 2026-07-18) is
        superseded by this chapter as authority. Keep the habitat note
        as a pointer / human-readable mirror, not a second source of truth.

        =========================================================
        LAYERING
        =========================================================
        - libs/workout/lib.pp     — package workout/… (seed on system/main)
        - data_rows types         — workout-session, workout-exercise
        - Routes via (route …)    — /workout and session/run paths
        - Optional nav entry      — ui/menu pin or seed menu link
        - OCaml                   — existing CRUD/date/random prims only;
                                    no new kernel prims required for v1

        Programs are CODE (+ optional doc templates), not table rows:
          each structured program owns a plan / run / capture triplet.
        Free-form sessions still use the same journal types.

        =========================================================
        THREE MODELS CONSIDERED (and the choice)
        =========================================================
        M1. Pure document
            One sexp/json object is the whole workout (plan + results).
            Good fluidity; bad cross-session volume queries unless every
            consumer understands every dialect.

        M2. Pure tables
            workouts + exercises [+ sets] only.
            Good queries; bad fit for ladders/intervals/emoms/dice and
            program-specific structure (wide nullable columns forever).

        M3. Hybrid (CHOSEN)
            Fluid document for prescription + live run state;
            standardized session + exercise fact rows for the journal;
            capture projects document → facts.
            Programs may be weird. Facts answer a closed question set.

        =========================================================
        JOURNAL QUESTIONS (closed fact schema derives from these)
        =========================================================
        - Which days did I train?
        - Which program / intensity?
        - How much volume of exercise X (optionally at load Y) in range Z?
        - What is the history of a single session?
        - Did I finish, abandon, or leave in progress?
        - What notes / how did it feel?

        Anything not required by those questions stays inside the
        fluid document (rungs, intervals, dice, rest schemes, UI cursor).

        =========================================================
        DATA MODEL (v1)
        =========================================================
        Types (deftype on load; fields are documentation + form UI).
        Each row is ONE tree (JSON object in data_rows.fields). Nested
        program variance lives under doc/params/progress/detail — never
        new top-level columns per program.

        workout-session
          date            string YYYY-MM-DD
          program         string  ; "ksk" | "qd" | "free" | …
          intensity       string  ; "easy" | "medium" | "hard" | "" 
                                  ; (NOT named "type" — overloaded elsewhere)
          state           string  ; in_progress | complete | abandoned
          notes           string
          doc             string  ; JSON/sexp-print of the fluid workout
                                  ; tree (plan + live progress). Source of
                                  ; structural truth for resume/replay.
          duration_sec    string int optional
          author          string optional  ; whoami at create; v1 may be ""
                                           ; (data_rows still shared)

        workout-exercise   ; QUERY GRAIN — projected journal facts
          session_id      uuid string of workout-session
          exercise        string  ; canonical name, e.g. "Snatch L", "Swing"
          weight          string number  ; "" if bodyweight / unset
          unit            string  ; "kg" | "lb" | ""  (normalize in capture)
          reps            string int     ; TOTAL completed reps (not per-set)
          notes           string
          detail          string optional JSON/sexp-print tree for
                                  per-set or program-specific breakdown
                                  when a program chooses to keep it

        NO per-set fact table in v1.
        NO side column — unilateral work uses naming ("Snatch L" / "Snatch R")
          so aggregation stays a simple group-by on exercise name.
        NO separate "program definitions" table — programs are code
          (and templates inside plan functions / doc skeletons).
         NO extra per-type ACL — the RLS floor scopes rows to their author
           (data.u.<user>.*), with the data.shared.* seed readable by all.
          Multi-user content isolation is multi-user.permissions later.
        Orphan exercise rows (missing session) show under a virtual
        "(orphan)" bucket in UI; agents can repair.

        Field print form:
          On-row storage may be JSON (current data_rows convention).
          Conceptually every nested value is a sexp tree. Package helpers
          MUST hide hand-built JSON strings from call sites
          (workout/session-fields, workout/exercise-fields, dict-set*).

        =========================================================
        FLUID DOCUMENT SHAPE (open envelope, closed top-level)
        =========================================================
        session.doc is a tree. Recommended envelope (keys stable;
        interior free):

          {
            "program": "ksk",
            "intensity": "hard",
            "params": { ... program-specific knobs ... },
            "progress": { ... live cursor / elapsed / side ... },
            "blocks": [ ... free structure: ladders, intervals, pairs ... ]
          }

        Examples (conceptual sexps; JSON equivalent is fine):

          ;; Kettlebell Simple & Sinister-style hard day cursor
          (workout-doc
            (program ksk)
            (intensity hard)
            (params (top-rung 5) (time-cap-min 20)
                    (load 24 kg) (exercise Snatch))
            (progress (rung 3) (side L) (elapsed-sec 740))
            (blocks
              (ladder (rungs 1 2 3 4 5) (switch each-rung))))

          ;; Free session
          (workout-doc
            (program free)
            (blocks
              (pair snatch (sets 5) (reps 2) (load 24 kg))
              (pair front-squat (sets 3) (reps 5) (load 60 kg))
              (interval row (rounds 10) (on 30) (off 30))))

        Plan generators produce docs (or doc skeletons).
        Run mode mutates progress inside doc (and may append detail).
        Capture reads doc (+ any explicit log events) and projects facts.

        =========================================================
        CAPTURE PROJECTION CONTRACT
        =========================================================
        Bridge rule:
          doc  --capture-->  session top-level fields + N exercise facts

        Requirements:
          - Idempotent per session: re-running capture replaces or
            upserts exercise facts for that session_id; it must not
            double-count volume on resume/refresh.
          - Totals win: workout-exercise.reps is aggregate completed work.
          - Program-specific structure stays in session.doc (and optional
            exercise.detail); not exploded into new fact columns.
          - Canonicalize exercise names and units in capture (title case
            policy is package-defined; document in lib.pp).
          - Abandoned/in_progress sessions may already have partial facts
            from live writes; complete() finalizes state and may re-project.

        Hybrid flavor for v1: H3 + H1
          - Per-program capture functions (H3)
          - Structured sessions always retain full doc (H1)
          - Free/quick-log may build a minimal doc from facts (still store it)

        =========================================================
        PROGRAM ARCHITECTURE
        =========================================================
        Each structured program owns a function triplet under workout/:

          (workout/<prog>-plan intensity-or-params) -> doc tree
          (workout/<prog>-run session-id)           -> HTML (live UI)
          (workout/<prog>-capture session-id)       -> session + facts

        Day intensities are DATA inside one algorithm when structure
        matches (e.g. KSK easy/medium/hard = top rung + time cap params).
        Split functions only when day types differ structurally.

        Intensity map example (package data, not tables):
          ksk:
            easy   -> top-rung 3, time-cap-min 10
            medium -> top-rung 4, time-cap-min 15
            hard   -> top-rung 5, time-cap-min 20

        Macro strategy:
          defprogram generating plan/run/capture is DEFERRED until ~3
          real programs exist (compress repetition, don't anticipate).
          Prefer quasiquote if/when language lands; hand-built list
          expansions are error-prone (see language macro feedback).

        v1 programs (suggested ship order):
          1. free   — quick log + optional simple blocks (always first)
          2. ksk    — ladder / time-cap runner (proves live run + projection)
          3. qd     — optional second structured program (dice + aggregates)
        Do not block journal MVP on ksk/qd polish — free log must work alone.

        =========================================================
        LIVE RUN / RESUME
        =========================================================
        - Creating a structured session stores state=in_progress and doc.
        - Live writes: each completed rung/exercise POSTs soon so a dead
          browser loses little; update doc.progress and upsert facts.
        - Timer UI may embed a small JS widget (precedent: weather/script);
          server remains authority for logged work.
        - htmx for step transitions (complete rung → swap next step).
        - Dice / random can be server-side (find-random or equivalent).
        - Resume: load in_progress session by id (or latest for program),
          re-enter run UI from doc.progress.
        - Cleanup: list/filter abandoned in_progress older than N days;
          mark abandoned via explicit UI/agent action (no silent delete).

        =========================================================
        PACKAGE API (workout/ prefix)
        =========================================================
        Sessions:
          (workout/session-list [limit]) -> list of (id . fields)
          (workout/session id) -> fields | ()
          (workout/session-create program intensity [date] [doc]) -> id
          (workout/session-update id fields-dict) -> id | ()
          (workout/session-complete id [notes]) -> id
          (workout/session-abandon id) -> id
          (workout/session-in-progress [program]) -> id | ()

        Exercises (facts):
          (workout/exercises session-id) -> list
          (workout/exercise-log session-id exercise weight unit reps
                                [notes] [detail]) -> id
            ;; upsert policy documented in lib.pp (by id or by
            ;; session+exercise+weight+unit for live rungs)
          (workout/exercise-delete id) -> id | ()

        Queries:
          (workout/volume exercise [from-date] [to-date] [weight] [unit])
            -> total reps (number) or printable structure
          (workout/history [from-date] [to-date] [limit]) -> sessions
          (workout/session-summary id) -> session + exercises structure
          (workout/exercise-names [limit]) -> distinct names for autocomplete

        Doc helpers:
          (workout/doc-parse s) -> dict/tree
          (workout/doc-get doc key) / (workout/doc-set doc key val)
          (workout/project session-id) -> re-run capture for program

        Programs (v1+):
          (workout/programs) -> list of program ids/titles available
          (workout/<prog>-plan …)
          (workout/<prog>-run session-id)    ; may be HTML page fn
          (workout/<prog>-capture session-id)

        HTML / routes:
          (route "/workout" "workout/home-page")
          (route "/workout/session" "workout/session-page")
          (route "/workout/run" "workout/run-page")
          (route "/workout/log" "workout/log-page")   ; quick log / edit facts
            (route "/workout/today" "workout/today-page") ; filmstrip pane: agenda for gated programs
            (route "/workout/chart" "workout/chart-page") ; filmstrip pane: all sets chart
          Exact query keys implementation discretion; prefer
            ?id=uuid & ?program= & ?intensity=

        Naming:
          package directory libs/workout/
          binding prefix workout/
          types workout-session / workout-exercise

        Data functions take explicit args (safe from /api/eval).
        HTTP handlers are separate and thin.

        =========================================================
        HYPERMEDIA UI
        =========================================================
        /workout
          - recent sessions (date, program, intensity, state, short volume)
          - Start bar: program select + intensity (when applicable) + start
          - Continue card if in_progress exists
          - link to quick log (free)

        /workout/session?id=
          - session header + notes + state actions (complete/abandon)
          - exercise fact table
          - add/edit fact row (quick correction)
          - if program structured and in_progress: Continue run

        /workout/run?id=
          - program-specific live UI from doc.progress
          - complete-step controls POST → update doc + facts → swap UI
          - timer widget as needed

        /workout/log (optional alias of free capture)
          - date, notes
          - repeatable exercise rows (name, weight, unit, reps)
          - save → session complete (or in_progress if want multi-step)

        Mobile-first: large tap targets during run; minimal chrome.
        Use existing product theme classes. No new OCaml CSS required.

        =========================================================
        SEED / NAV
        =========================================================
        - seed_stdlib: load-library "workout" after calendar
          (needs date-today; order free as long as std/html exists)
        - ui/menu: Workout → /workout on system seed when easy;
          personal may pin. Not a kernel nav hard-code.

        =========================================================
        AGENT ACCESS
        =========================================================
        Image is the API:
          pp_eval '(load-library "workout")'
          pp_eval '(workout/session-create "free" "" )'
          pp_eval '(workout/exercise-log id "Swing" "53" "lb" "75")'
          pp_eval '(workout/session-complete id)'
          pp_eval '(workout/volume "Swing" "2026-07-01" "2026-07-31")'
        No workout-specific REST. Bulk backfill via agent loops.

        =========================================================
        NON-GOALS (v1)
        =========================================================
        - Wearables, HR zones, GPS, Apple Health / Google Fit sync
        - Social feed, followers, public leaderboards
        - Plate calculator / 1RM formulas as core (may be helpers later)
        - Full periodization planner / mesocycle engine
        - Per-set fact table / side column / equipment inventory
        - defprogram macro before ~3 programs exist
        - Branch-scoped journal rows (shared data_rows by design)
        - OCaml system pages for training UX
        - Treating JSON vs sexp print form as different product models

   |))
  )

  (subsection model
   (doc "Hybrid: workout-session + workout-exercise facts; session.doc fluid tree")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "load-library defines workout-session and workout-exercise")
    (smoke "session-create stores program intensity state date doc")
    (smoke "exercise-log attaches facts to session_id with total reps")
    (smoke "unilateral names work without a side column")))

  (subsection document-and-capture
   (doc "Fluid doc envelope + idempotent projection to exercise facts")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "structured session retains doc through run updates")
    (smoke "capture/project does not double-count on second run")
    (smoke "volume query uses facts only, not doc scraping")))

  (subsection programs
   (doc "plan/run/capture triplets; free first; ksk/qd optional structured")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "workout/programs lists at least free")
    (smoke "free quick-log creates complete session + facts")
    (smoke "optional: ksk plan returns doc with params+blocks")))

  (subsection ui
   (doc "Routes /workout, session, run, log; resume in_progress")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "GET /workout 200 after load-library")
    (smoke "start + complete free session visible in recent list")
    (smoke "in_progress shows continue entry point")))

  (subsection agent-access
   (doc "pp_eval workout/… as the API")
   (status implemented)
   (verify
    (smoke "pp_eval workout/session-list and workout/volume"))
  )

  (subsection nutrition
   (doc "libs/food — daily meal templates + calorie/macros logging: the body-format sibling of the workout session doc (same day-living family, weight alongside food/calories)")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/food/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "(load-library \"food\") defines food/* helpers; food/add-template logs a meal row keyed by day-type + meal"))
  )

  (subsection program-state-and-gates
   (doc "Spec docs/plans/workout-gating.md. Outcome-driven programs (KSF C&J, run/walk, SCT core, Quicksilver stretch) cannot pre-materialize calendars: the next session is a pure function of stored program state + date. Two additive types: workout-program-state (one ACTIVE row per program; new writes supersede, history preserved) and workout-gate (the asserted-gate ledger: checkpoints passed, soreness flags, range-ownership — derived gates are NEVER stored, they recompute from journal facts at capture). workout/suggest generates today's session on demand (pure, idempotent); workout/session-complete evaluates gates and turns the state over; workout/gate-status summarizes cursor + ledger for agents. Nested lists are not legal dict values — summaries render as strings (see gates-summary). Toy program \"toy\" (advance after every 3 completions) proves the loop end-to-end via pp_eval. Calendar untouched — ksk1 keeps its scheduler.")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (build "dune build @all")
    (smoke "(load-library \"workout\") defines workout-program-state + workout-gate and machinery fns")
    (smoke "suggest toy renders the fresh-session doc; 3 completed toy sessions turn state over to level 2 in gate-status")
    (smoke "abandoned sessions do not advance derived gates")
    (smoke "workout/gate-assert records ledger rows; gate-status renders them as a summary string"))

  (subsection ksf
   (doc "Kettlebells StrongFirst C&J (Pavel) built on the gating machinery. Plan A: single-bell long-cycle both days, sets every 30s (weak arm on top of the minute), rep ladder CJ -> CJC -> CJCJ -> CJCJC -> CJCJCJ. A cleared session (Duration fact >= 30 min) advances one +clean/+jerk step; the ladder end hands off to Plan B; 6 short sessions in a row flip to Plan B (RM-retest doctrine). Plan B: cleans day / jerks day (Fri = C, Sun = J under the 2-day variant), sets of 3 -> 4 -> 5 per 30s capped at P5. Clock rail: every 8 completed sessions a 2-session deload (one bell lighter, -4kg/-9lb) holds the pattern. workout/ksf-configure after the LC RM test (weaker arm 6-12RM; targets men 40% BW / women 30% BW max 24kg). Started sessions carry today's suggestion doc so deload/pattern flags ride into gates. Get-ups are side dishes: v1 users log them as facts (LC C&J L/R split + Duration are the recognized exercises).")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "ksf-configure seeds state; suggest renders LCCJ docs on Fri/Sun, OFF otherwise; Plan B suggests C on Fri and J on Sun")
    (smoke "cleared sessions advance CJ -> CJC -> ... -> CJCJCJ -> handoff to Plan B at P3")
    (smoke "stall: six short sessions flip phase A to Plan B with retest note")
    (smoke "deload rail: since_deload >= 8 starts deload_left=2; deload sessions suggest bell -4kg, hold pattern, decrement deload_left")
    (smoke "home start card creates ksf sessions carrying today's suggestion doc"))
  )

  (subsection run5k
   (doc "Run-to-5K walk/run builder on the gating machinery. Week table (18 weeks): Friday = ratio session (shifting jog:walk ratio in a fixed box), Sunday = long session (box grows 20 to ~45 min, w18 = RACE). Deload weeks are table-encoded repeats. Gates: each completed session ticks in_week; after 2 the week turns over - unless a sore gate was asserted mid-week, which repeats the week. Sore asserts are consumed via a monotonic ledger marker (sore_mark) so a mid-week flag survives the intervening session's eval. Talk test (conversational) is the intensity ceiling; maps to workout/gate-assert for the human flow.")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "run5k-configure seeds week 1; suggest renders A goal Fri, B goal Sun, OFF otherwise")
    (smoke "clean week of 2 completions advances the week; week 5 Sunday renders 60/60/9")
    (smoke "mid-week sore assert repeats the week exactly once (marker consumed on the decision)")
    (smoke "home start card creates run5k sessions carrying today's goal doc"))
  )
  (subsection sct
   (doc "Systematic Core Training (Geoff Neupert) on the gating machinery. Three sequential phase sub-cursors - stability (12 session columns) -> strength (9) -> power (12) - driven by the session tables (dead bug columns, hollow hold seconds, leg-raise reps, tuck/L-sit hold seconds, hanging reps, ground holds, kickstand->SL deadlifts). Friday = floor work, Sunday = floor + supported/hanging (bar + 16-32kg bells available, hanging selectable straightaway); ground-based enters at strength S7; power = Sunday carry blocks (24kg / 2x24kg, rotating suitcase -> rack -> overhead -> bottoms-up -> farmers -> double rack -> double overhead, minutes 7 -> 10, RPE waves 7/8/9). Micro-dose on OFF days (breathing + dead bugs + neck drills; submax floor set in strength phase) - the daily practice, never the progressing surface. Session columns advance on every completed sct session, capped at the phase benchmark column; promotion is EXPLICIT: benchmark day renders benchmark_due, then (workout/sct-promote) asserts the ledger (stability-exit / strength-exit) and moves the phase.")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "sct-configure seeds stability s1; suggest renders session-table content per phase and day")
    (smoke "12 completed sessions cap at the benchmark column; suggest marks benchmark_due")
    (smoke "sct-promote asserts stability-exit / strength-exit and moves the phase")
    (smoke "OFF days render the daily micro-dose (stability menu; submax extra in strength phase)"))
  )
  (subsection stretch
   (doc "Quicksilver leapfrog on the gating machinery. Cycle A advances the Front Split (light: reverse hamstring + kneeling lunge prying; medium: pulses+holds to 10/30s; heavy: extended isometric) while the Loaded Straddle holds at Cossack pulses; Cycle B flips. Rhythm rail: Sunday = advancing slot (Pulses+Holds, or Extended Isometric on alternating Sundays once the range is owned - upgrade-only iso_unlocked), Wednesday = medium maintenance slot, everything else prying only. Promotion: own-the-range asserts unlock the iso tool (monotonic ledger marker); (workout/stretch-flip) is explicit when the advancing goal is achieved. Journaling is sparse by design - Sunday/Wednesday slots journaled, daily prying is day-activity. Scene family: all four sct/ksf/run5k/stretch programs + the natively-seeded ksk1-3 live in one journal with shared volume queries (LC C&J, Snatch L/R, Dead Bug reps, Duration minutes ...).")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/workout/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "stretch-configure seeds cycle A; suggest renders Front Split pulses on Sunday (extended iso only after own-the-range), Cossack maintenance on Wednesday, light prying otherwise")
    (smoke "own-the-range asserts unlock iso_upgrade-only (never downgrades)")
    (smoke "stretch-flip asserts cycle-achieved and swaps the leapfrog cycle; cycle B suggests Straddle advancement on Sunday")
    (smoke "home start card creates stretch sessions carrying the slot doc"))
  )
  )
 )
)
